{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"agent_message","text":"The strongest earlier gain came from preserving target-field matches in history summaries. The latest nonlinear event encoder did not beat the incumbent (0.830376 versus 0.830379 macro AUC), so that result gives little support for adding generic event complexity.\n\nI’m testing a narrower limitation: the model summarizes each field match separately, which can obscure whether two fields matched on the same historical event. I’ll compare joint-match content and counts with estimates built from their separate marginals, using four matched controls."}}
