e failures and stop for hard deadline, integrity failure or no useful admissible remaining experiment. Current proposal establishes neither a performance improvement nor completed assessment.'\n }\n}\nvariant_specs=[\n ('pair_joint_both','candidate.py','candidate','joint','joint'),\n ('pair_joint_content','pair_joint_content.py','control','joint','factorized'),\n ('pair_joint_counts','pair_joint_counts.py','control','factorized','joint'),\n ('pair_marginal_both','pair_marginal_control.py','control','factorized','factorized')\n]\nvariants=[]\nfor name,file,role,content,count in variant_specs:\n source=Path(file).read_text(); tree=ast.parse(source)\n config=next(ast.literal_eval(n.value) for n in tree.body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='CONFIG' for t in n.targets))\n variants.append({'name':name,'file':file,'role':role,'config':config,'note':f'Pair content={content}; pair count={count}. Standalone module; 54240 added parameters; unchanged token count, inherited initialization and frozen recipe. Same FP32 summary kernels and equal bank dimensions across all cells; selected backward cost may differ. SHA256 {hashlib.sha256(source.encode()).hexdigest()}. Syntax/import/CONFIG-default and normalized factorial-source checks passed, plus15 inherited helper-method AST comparisons and a standard-library scalar algebra oracle (200 signed/sparse/empty cases, balanced routing and controlled joint-versus-marginal examples). These are static/algebraic checks only. Torch/numpy are unavailable; no training or installation ran. Actual forward/backward, masking, BF16, parent-equivalence, parameters and measured costs remain pending on host.'})\ndef assessment(knowledge_id,decision,rationale,mechanism,names,difference):\n return {'knowledge_id':knowledge_id,'decision':decision,'rationale':rationale,'transformed_mechanism':mechanism,'variant_names':names,'nearest_work_difference':difference,'falsifier':'A source-to-code link is provenance only. No external effectiveness, originality or mechanism-transfer claim follows without the local matched contrasts, numerical validity, measured costs and consequential paired repetitions.'}\nnames=[x['name'] for x in variants]\nassessments=[\n assessment('unirank-method-hiformer','considered','Pinned forward inspected: post-pooling field/task tokenization is a close architectural reference. Prior pooled_silu did not beat the incumbent.','No new HiFormer component adopted; preserve the incumbent interaction while changing explicit pair summaries.',[], 'No hierarchical heterogeneous block or task-token readout replacement.'),\n assessment('unirank-method-est','considered','Pinned forward and interaction inspected. Direct event retrieval is an alternative for recovering detail, but changes retrieval/backbone and cost together.','No EST component adopted in this representation-only factorial.',[], 'No event-token cross-attention stack or feature-specific FFN addition.'),\n assessment('unirank-method-infnet','used','Inherited incumbent feedback memory is retained, and its relation to the pinned feedback-masked hubs was inspected. Joint/collapsed local results do not prove generic feedback separation helps.','Existing one-way read from compressed feedback/time memory remains identical in every variant; the newly changed mechanism is item-field conjunction summaries.',names,'No INFNet hub/broadcast stack, task queries or original/proxy reproduction is claimed.'),\n assessment('unirank-method-tokenformer','considered','Pinned nonlinear event tokenizer inspected; the latest four local placement trials were reviewed and none exceeded the incumbent.','The previous event-composition branch is not inherited. Test pair-mask binding instead of another nonlinear event encoder.',[], 'No sequence/target MLP tokenizer, separators or raw-event attention backbone is added.'),\n assessment('unirank-method-hemix','considered','Resolved the card to address the previous undocumented retrieval. Fixed/feature-conditioned queries and recent/earlier partitions are a different candidate mechanism; card provenance alone is insufficient for a priority claim.','No HeMix component adopted; existing rank bins and local activation remain.',[], 'No new query family, recent/earlier partition rule or low-rank heterogeneous mixer.'),\n assessment('unirank-method-onetrans','considered','Previous knowledge usage considered repeated mixed sequence/static attention. The current source change does not adopt that direction, and its original paper was not audited here.','No OneTrans change adopted; retain the incumbent backbone to isolate conjunction sources.',[], 'No progressive sequence reduction, repeated mixed-attention layers or token-specific FFNs.')\n]\nproposal={'study':study,'parent_trial':parent,'variants':variants,'knowledge_assessments':assessments}\nPath('proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(proposal,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Wrote proposal.json with',len(variants),'variants and',len(assessments),'knowledge assessments.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport ast, hashlib, json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nprotocol='427fc51900560816321ba9bbc170639eb26625972df75b22e3c47d523c363748'\nparent='g0-r0011-memory_joint_collapsed'\nfixed=[\n 'Pinned data identity, released fields, official train/validation split and official_offline visibility; history limit 100.',\n 'Frozen one-pass recipe, batch8192, seed20262027, AdamW/Adagrad, BF16, dense-only gradient clip10, four unweighted BCEs and all-four-task macro AUC selection.',\n 'Every inherited embedding, local-activation weight, moment/content/feedback path, memory module, JointBlock, tower, token position, token validity and readout width.',\n 'All 15 unordered pairs of the six item fields, five temporal bins, pair-bank dimensions, zero initialization, deterministic routing, both joint and marginal forward computations.'\n]\nconfounds=[\n 'Equal parameter count does not equal equal effective function class. Joint and marginal sources have different sparsity, distributions and selected backward graphs; report actual training, inference and peak memory.',\n 'Learned event weights and multi-field embeddings may already encode some conjunctions implicitly. This tests an explicit representation, not proof that the whole incumbent cannot represent co-occurrence.',\n 'Encoded field hierarchies can make some pairs deterministic or redundant; missing/OOV codes may coincide. Positive IDs exclude declared padding but do not guarantee real entity identity.',\n 'FP32 sums precede host-autocast projections in all cells, but numerical/autograd paths can still differ. The shared dense gradient clip can couple the added branch to inherited optimization.',\n 'One frozen seed on repeatedly consulted validation data provides preliminary local evidence, not significance or holdout confirmation.'\n]\ncontrasts=[\n {\n  'parent_ref':parent,\n  'intervention':'pair_joint_both (joint content, joint count) versus pair_marginal_both (factorized content, factorized count): primary capacity-matched replacement contrast.',\n  'control':'Both variants own the same 15 bias-free [113,32] pair maps. The control derives pair content/counts solely from marginal relation summaries; it is active, not a zero branch. The recorded incumbent is the historical no-added-branch reference, not a capacity-matched control.',\n  'held_fixed':fixed,'remaining_confounds':confounds,\n  'decision_if_supported':'If the joint variant beats both this active control and the incumbent under the declared macro-AUC rule, retain a provisional explicit-conjunction direction; examine content/count contrasts and reserve paired repetitions before a mechanism claim.',\n  'decision_if_not_supported':'If both active variants improve similarly, attribute evidence to added parameterization/optimization rather than same-event binding. If neither improves, keep the incumbent and report a negative implementation result; do not refute all conjunctive representations.'\n },\n {\n  'parent_ref':parent,\n  'intervention':'Content main effects: pair_joint_both minus pair_joint_counts, and pair_joint_content minus pair_marginal_both.',\n  'control':'Hold the count source at joint or factorized respectively; change only the content source between exact same-event intersection sums and symmetric marginal estimates.',\n  'held_fixed':fixed,'remaining_confounds':confounds,\n  'decision_if_supported':'Consistent positive content contrasts favor preserving which item/action content occurred in the intersection, rather than just intersection frequency. Repeat the closest pair if consequential.',\n  'decision_if_not_supported':'A count-only gain supports an occupancy representation, not content binding. Mixed signs require reporting an interaction or weak support rather than averaging into a universal content claim.'\n },\n {\n  'parent_ref':parent,\n  'intervention':'Count main effects: pair_joint_both minus pair_joint_content, and pair_joint_counts minus pair_marginal_both. Report the factorial interaction A(j,j)-A(j,f)-A(f,j)+A(f,f).',\n  'control':'Hold the content source fixed; change log1p intersection count to log1p(n_r*n_s/n). Every cell preserves the parent marginal counts and temporal masks.',\n  'held_fixed':fixed,'remaining_confounds':confounds,\n  'decision_if_supported':'Consistent count effects suggest explicit joint occupancy matters; an interaction restricts the conclusion to the corresponding combined representation.',\n  'decision_if_not_supported':'Do not retain exact count channels on a mechanism argument if their effects are absent or adverse; choose only by the frozen four-task validation rule and document trade-offs.'\n }\n]\nstudy={\n 'id':'g0-t000-pairwise-target-match-content-count-factorial',\n 'protocol_ref':protocol,\n 'evidence_refs':[\n  'baseline-din','g0-r0000-recency_slots','g0-r0001-grouped_recency','g0-r0002-replica_seven',\n  'g0-r0003-relation_content_counts','g0-r0003-relation_content_only','g0-r0003-relation_counts_only','g0-r0003-replica_control',\n  'g0-r0004-joint_feedback_counts','g0-r0004-zero_feedback_counts',\n  'g0-r0008-relation_bank','g0-r0008-rotated_bank','g0-r0009-relation_content','g0-r0009-rotated_content',\n  'g0-r0010-feedback_bound','g0-r0010-feedback_factorized','g0-r0010-feedback_zero',\n  'g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate','g0-r0011-memory_factorized_separate',parent,'g0-r0011-memory_factorized_collapsed',\n  'g0-r0012-event_silu','g0-r0012-pooled_silu','g0-r0012-event_linear','g0-r0012-pooled_linear'\n ],\n 'question':(\n  'Can explicit same-event conjunctions of target-field matches improve the current first-order relation representation? '\n  'The supplied 53-entry trajectory index contains successful runs, not failed execution receipts. The strongest early representation contrast was relation_content_counts=0.82757048 versus replica_control=0.81978673; content-only=0.82624720 and counts-only=0.82007791. '\n  'Relation-specific banks also exceeded rotated controls, while adding joint feedback counts regressed (g0-r0004-joint_feedback_counts=0.82656761 versus zero_feedback_counts=0.82757048). '\n  'Later feedback binding was inconsistent: feedback_bound=0.82980946 versus factorized=0.82999920; joint versus factorized memory changes sign between separate and collapsed layouts. '\n  'The incumbent is joint/collapsed memory at 0.8303789179. The latest event_silu=0.8303761499, pooled_silu=0.8303331335, event_linear=0.8302301477 and pooled_linear=0.8303185690 did not surpass it; linear placements, algebraically commuting, still differ numerically. '\n  'These observations favor a targeted representation contrast rather than asserting that arbitrary event nonlinearity helps. Source inspection shows six overlapping field-equality masks summarized separately in five bins; no explicit pair intersection is retained. '\n  'Joint pair support/covariance in the actual data is unavailable here. The idea is motivated by this code limitation, not an invented prevalence measurement. The recorded length slices are descriptive: incumbent empty_history n6444 (buy positives13), history1_16 n461684, history17_64 n1001754, history_gt64 n1401885. Differences across those populations are not causal effects of length.'\n ),\n 'hypothesis':(\n  'When separate target-field matches occur on different versus the same historical event, explicit pair-intersection content and occupancy can provide useful evidence beyond marginal summaries. '\n  'Preserve all existing first-order, rank, feedback and static paths; add pair information as zero-start residual updates to the same relation tokens before joint interaction. '\n  'An active marginal-information replacement with the same parameters tests whether any gain depends on same-event binding. '\n  'The auxiliary labels match user/category/brand over24h, so category-brand conjunction is a plausible member of the fixed 15-pair family, not a claim of advertisement conversion attribution or a premeasured special case.'\n ),\n 'nearest_work':[\n  {'source_ref':'paper:din','verification':'read','difference':'Archived v4 primary text lines55-83 describes target-conditioned weighted behavior pooling. Local activation and signed sums are inherited. This study adds explicit pair-equality summaries and matched marginal replacements; it does not reproduce DIN exactly or claim priority.'},\n  {'source_ref':'unirank-code:HiFormer','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned commit90bb99a forward lines113-144 pools history before heterogeneous field/task tokenization. Retain the local incumbent interaction/towers and test conjunction summaries; do not adopt HiFormer blocks or import its benchmark performance.'},\n  {'source_ref':'unirank-code:EST','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned forward lines119-155 and stack lines198-205 retain event tokens for sequence-to-field retrieval. Here the raw sequence backbone is unchanged; conjunctive masks produce summaries injected into existing tokens, with no extra retrieval layers.'},\n  {'source_ref':'unirank-code:INFNet','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned lines123-160 initialize feedback-masked sequence hubs and run multi-layer aggregation/broadcast. The incumbent one-way feedback memory is related inherited work, not an INFNet reproduction. The new mechanism concerns pairs of item-field matches, not task hubs.'},\n  {'source_ref':'unirank-code:TokenFormer','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned tokenizer lines161-209 applies nonlinear maps to sequence and target events before concatenation. The preceding local placement factorial was inconclusive and did not beat the incumbent; this proposal does not add that nonlinear event encoder.'},\n  {'source_ref':'paper:dmr','verification':'read','difference':'Only the pinned author README was available, including its category/brand/behavior-only history warning. Full paper unavailable; no detailed mechanism or novelty comparison is established. The released local inputs include six advertisement fields, so external task equivalence is not assumed.'}\n ],\n 'inherited_components':[\n  'Complete g0-r0011-memory_joint_collapsed architecture represented by initial candidate.py: feature embeddings, static fields and current target; sanitized historical IDs and excluded target action.',\n  'Shared DIN local activation, five valid-rank windows, seven global/field-match relation channels and explicit marginal counts.',\n  'Linear rank moments, residual copy, relation-specific moment/content banks and factorized feedback-content bank.',\n  'Twenty-slot joint/collapsed feedback memory, one JointBlock, four separate task towers, raw static/global pooled bypass and default training loss.',\n  'Host-owned data, visibility, identity, training, scoring and resource contracts; no borrowed external performance claim.'\n ],\n 'proposed_difference':(\n  'For every unordered pair (r,s) of the six item-field equality masks and every one of the five temporal bins, compute C_rs=sum_i 1_r(i)1_s(i)w_i v_i/sqrt(7) and n_rs=sum_i1_r(i)1_s(i). '\n  'The factorized count is n_r*n_s/max(n,1); factorized content is (n_s*C_r+n_r*C_s)/(2*max(n,1)), using recomputed FP32 marginal sums with the same signed weights and full item/action values. '\n  'All four cells compute both sources in FP32, independently choose joint/factorized content and count, concatenate content with log1p(count)/log101, and project through 15 independent zero-initialized bias-free [113,32] maps shared over windows. '\n  'Route each pair output to its two existing relation slots with coefficient1/sqrt5. No global-slot update, new attention key, identity token or readout dimension is introduced. '\n  'Exactly54240 additional parameters are estimated from frozen six fields and embedding16; expected total33076645 and dense1283429, pending host confirmation. No random draw is introduced after inherited initialization. '\n  'Zero bank gives the parent initial function algebraically; it is not an empirical parent-equivalence result. Marginal estimates are explicit controls, not an assertion that field matches are independent. '\n  'This is a local experimental difference. Originality relative to the full literature remains unverified.'\n ),\n 'predictions':[\n  'Primary: pair_joint_both should exceed pair_marginal_both and the incumbent on validation macro AUC if explicit conjunctions add useful information under the fixed single-pass recipe. Rank all four cells by the existing tie-breakers; report macro Logloss and all task AUC/Logloss deltas against both incumbent and baseline-din, without an undeclared task veto.',\n  'Content and count effects are distinguishable through the declared 2x2 contrasts. A content claim requires joint-content effects at matched count source; a count claim requires the converse. Effects dependent on the other factor are interactions, not universal mechanisms.',\n  'Predeclared descriptive slices remain the supplied history bins: empty,1-16,17-64,>64. Report per-task positive/negative/sample counts; treat rare empty-history labels as insufficient for a strong claim. There is no expected direct pair-path contribution on empty histories; retraining may still change their predictions indirectly.',\n  'Host numerical gates, if provided by the authorized interface, should establish finite [B,1] probabilities for all four labels, gradients, FP32/BF16 behavior, zero-bank parent equivalence, identical inherited initial parameters/RNG state, and eval/cloned-state train invariance to masked IDs/actions/task masks and current action. Include L0, singleton, holey/full/all-empty masks, no matches and all matches. Real sample inputs and a Torch runtime are unavailable in this coding environment.',\n  'Exploratory pair support, joint-minus-marginal gaps and field hierarchy redundancy would distinguish useful conjunctions from 